  odds  a_i=2i-1             +nan -2.026e-03 -9.019e-04 -4.677e-04 -2.730e-04 -1.729e-04      3.000
  squares ~i^2               +nan -2.391e-02 -5.301e-03 +1.143e-03 +2.454e-04 -7.018e-05      6.333
  cubes ~i^3                 +nan +3.128e-01 +1.650e-01 +7.426e-02 -3.126e-02 -1.747e-02     26.333
  primes                     +nan -4.685e-03 -1.303e-03 -4.909e-05 -1.734e-04 -6.534e-05      5.349

  interpretation: for the lambda^2 law to be testable on a profile, dev at the centre
  must already be ~0. If it is not, Gamma itself is not the limit for that profile.

